@page "/about"
@layout Layout.MainLayout

<SeoHead Title="About Beldsoft | Practical Technology Consulting"
         Description="Learn how Beldsoft approaches software engineering and technology consulting for small and medium-sized businesses." Path="/about" />

<section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-hero-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">About Beldsoft</span><h1>Technical depth, translated into practical decisions.</h1></div><p class="lead">Beldsoft helps growing organizations use software as an advantage—not inherit more complexity, cost, or risk.</p></div></section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Our purpose</span><h2>Make experienced software engineering accessible to businesses that need results.</h2></div>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>Small and medium-sized organizations often reach a point where generic software, disconnected tools, or aging applications begin to constrain the business. The problem is rarely solved by adding technology without a plan.</p>
            <p>Beldsoft brings architecture, engineering, integration, automation, and delivery thinking together. We begin with the business outcome, make tradeoffs explicit, and build solutions that the organization can understand and sustain.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Working principles</span><h2>What clients should expect from the engagement.</h2></div>
        <div class="card-grid card-grid-3">
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Business context first</h3><p>Technology decisions are tied to users, operations, risk, and the outcome that matters.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Plain-spoken advice</h3><p>Options and tradeoffs are explained clearly so decision-makers can act with confidence.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Responsible delivery</h3><p>Security, quality, maintainability, and operational ownership are considered from the start.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Incremental progress</h3><p>Work is shaped into reviewable stages that reduce uncertainty and expose value sooner.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Fit over fashion</h3><p>Tools are selected because they suit the problem—not because they are currently popular.</p></article>
            <article class="value-card"><h3>Honest boundaries</h3><p>Assumptions, dependencies, unknowns, and risks are made visible before they become surprises.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">A capable extension of your team</span><h2>Bring structure to your next software decision.</h2></div><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Request a consultation</a></div></section>
